## 4. Honest assessment of maturity

**Real, mature, buy-it now:** IP-audio DSP with fine-grained zoning (Q-SYS,
Biamp, Praesensa); STIPA measurement; Layer-1 acoustic materials with published
NRC/SAA data; sensory certification programs; commodity FIDS. A MWAA design
standard could specify all of these against numeric targets today without waiting
for any product roadmap.

**Real but early:** Beamformed loudspeaker arrays at airport scale (proven at
Frankfurt Central Station and event venues, not yet a mainline U.S. airport
reference); Auracast at gate scale (standard is shipping, ecosystem is thin but
growing fast); BLE-beacon boarding pushes via airline apps (works, but requires
airline concurrence).

**Hype more than substance:** "AI-driven" announcement generation; "smart"
sensor-driven quiet-mode automation without measured baseline; airport-branded
"silent" claims without measurement; sensory certifications marketed as design
standards.

**Genuinely missing:** A published, peer-reviewed airport quiet-terminal outcome
study that ties Layer 1–4 investment to measured passenger, employee, and
operational outcomes across seasons and irregular ops. If MWAA builds one, it
would be the reference.

